{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they broke off.</b> A term of removing a load — when they took them off their ears, they were found stripped of their earrings; דישקריי\"ר בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>The earrings of.</b> Like 'from the earrings of' — as in ״כְּצֵאתִי אֶת הָעִיר״ (Exodus 9) — from the city."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French deschireier, 'to tear off / strip away'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:03.545346094Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}